Threshold curve for KOSARAK on D_init, measured 2026-09-14 on ADMIN-PC with
experiments.ThresholdScan --grid. The submitted ladder {12, 6, 5, 5} is unusable on
this release: 6 and 5 both land at 0.030, so three of its four levels share one
threshold. These probes located the range the database actually separates over, and
the sweep 0.020 0.025 0.028 0.030 was chosen from them for 12 9 7 5 patterns.

0.019 is the wall, and it is the candidate cap rather than the clock, so it falls in
the same place on any machine. Twelve patterns is therefore a ceiling, not a choice.

